{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01X7wSts5q1CWve2Khrb3CGq","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd091-chown\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/chown: Change File Owner and Group\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  macOS ships a BSD chown that differs from GNU chown in recursive traversal flags,\n6\t  symlink handling, and OWNER:GROUP parsing. The Go implementation must match the\n7\t  Homebrew GNU reference binary (gchown, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all\n8\t  flag combinations, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n9\t\n10\tgoals:\n11\t  - G1: Change the owner and/or group of files using OWNER, OWNER:GROUP, OWNER:, :GROUP, or numeric UID:GID syntax.\n12\t  - G2: Support recursive ownership changes with -R and symlink traversal control.\n13\t  - G3: Verify functional parity against gchown via differential testing.\n14\t\n15\trequirements:\n16\t  R1:\n17\t    title: Ownership specification\n18\t    items:\n19\t      - R1.1:\n20\t          text: \"Must accept OWNER[:GROUP] syntax: OWNER changes only owner, OWNER:GROUP changes both, OWNER: changes owner and sets group to OWNER's login group, :GROUP changes only group.\"\n21\t      - R1.2:\n22\t          text: OWNER and GROUP may be names or numeric IDs. Must resolve names to IDs via the system user/group database.\n23\t      - R1.3:\n24\t          text: \"--reference=RFILE must set each FILE's owner and group to match RFILE's.\"\n25\t      - R1.4:\n26\t          text: Must exit 1 when any file cannot be accessed or the owner/group is invalid, printing an error to stderr, and continue processing remaining files.\n27\t\n28\t  R2:\n29\t    title: Recursive and symlink handling\n30\t    items:\n31\t      - R2.1:\n32\t          text: \"-R or --recursive must change ownership recursively for directories and their contents.\"\n33\t      - R2.2:\n34\t          text: \"-h or --no-dereference must change the symlink itself rather than the target.\"\n35\t      - R2.3:\n36\t          text: \"-H must follow symlinks on the command line only. -L must follow all symlinks. -P must never follow symlinks (default with -R).\"\n37\t\n38\t  R3:\n39\t    title: Output control and exit codes\n40\t    items:\n41\t      - R3.1:\n42\t          text: \"-v or --verbose must print a diagnostic for every file processed. -c or --changes must print only when changes are made. -f or --silent must suppress most errors.\"\n43\t      - R3.2:\n44\t          text: Must exit 0 when all files are processed successfully. Must exit 1 on any error.\n45\t      - R3.3:\n46\t          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n47\t\n48\tnon_goals:\n49\t  - cmd/chown does not implement --preserve-root.\n50\t  - cmd/chown does not implement --from=CURRENT_OWNER:CURRENT_GROUP conditional change.\n51\t\n52\tacceptance_criteria:\n53\t  - id: AC1\n54\t    criterion: \"chown user:staff file changes owner and group, matching gchown.\"\n55\t    traces:\n56\t      - R1.1\n57\t      - R1.2\n58\t  - id: AC2\n59\t    criterion: \"chown -R user dir recursively changes owner, matching gchown -R.\"\n60\t    traces:\n61\t      - R2.1\n62\t  - id: AC3\n63\t    criterion: \"chown :staff file changes only group, matching gchown.\"\n64\t    traces:\n65\t      - R1.1\n66\t  - id: AC4\n67\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gchown passes for all required test cases.\"\n68\t    traces:\n69\t      - R1.1\n70\t      - R1.2\n71\t      - R2.1\n72\t  - id: AC5\n73\t    criterion: \"cmd/chown compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n74\t    traces:\n75\t      - R1.1\n76\t      - R1.2\n77\t      - R1.3\n78\t      - R1.4\n79\t      - R2.1\n80\t      - R2.2\n81\t      - R2.3\n82\t      - R3.1\n83\t      - R3.2\n84\t      - R3.3\n85\t\n86\tpackage_contract:\n87\t  imports:\n88\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n89\t\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_015M4hu1QNDo6eeemKSaqPXw","session_id":"28576ec6-2aa4-4dfd-9a4a-73f493f2dc46","uuid":"9bb42e98-4b12-4f3f-9a78-c7c6ee19de88","timestamp":"2026-05-24T01:28:32.864Z"}
