{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015M4hu1QNDo6eeemKSaqPXw","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I've successfully read all four files. Here's a summary of what you have:\n\n## File Contents Summary\n\n**1. docs/specs/software-requirements/srd091-chown.yaml**\nThis is the Software Requirements Document for implementing `cmd/chown`. It specifies:\n- Must support ownership specification with OWNER[:GROUP] syntax, including numeric IDs\n- Must support --reference=RFILE to match another file's ownership\n- Must implement recursive (-R) and symlink handling flags (-h, -H, -L, -P)\n- Must support verbose (-v), changes (-c), and silent (-f) output modes\n- Exit code 0 on success, 1 on any error\n- Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler\n- Does NOT need --preserve-root or --from conditional changes\n\n**2. cmd/chmod/main.go**\nThe chmod implementation showing the pattern you should follow:\n- Parses arguments into options, mode, and files\n- Processes files with recursive support via filepath.WalkDir\n- Supports -v (verbose), -c (changes), -f (silent), -R (recursive), --reference\n- Uses os.Lstat for symlink-safe operations\n- Has applyAndReport function that applies changes and prints diagnostics\n- Includes formatErr for error formatting\n\n**3. cmd/chgrp/main.go**\nThe chgrp implementation that closely parallels what chown needs:\n- Parses arguments into options, group, and files\n- Supports -v, -c, -f, -R, -h (no-dereference), -H, -L, -P flags\n- Has resolveGID, lookupGroup, and gidToName helper functions\n- Uses os.Lchown / os.Chown with symlink mode logic\n- chownSingle for non-recursive, chownRecursive for -R flag\n- shouldFollowLink logic for -H/-L/-P flags\n- printDiagnostic and reportError functions\n- Includes sys.Stat and sys.Lstat for cross-platform file info\n\n**4. cmd/chgrp/chgrp_test.go**\nComprehensive differential testing framework:\n- Uses testutils.RunDiffTests to compare output against reference gchgrp\n- Tests all major code paths: basic changes, numeric GIDs, multiple files, references, recursion\n- Tests symlink handling (-h, -P, -H, -L variants)\n- Tests output modes (-v verbose, -c changes, -f silent)\n- Includes error cases (invalid group, missing operands, nonexistent files)\n- Helper functions: testGroups, setGroup, verifyGroup, normalizeBinaryName, sortLines\n- Uses reset functions to return files to original state between runs\n\nYou now have the template and pattern to implement cmd/chown, which will need to handle both owner and group changes (combining chmod-like modes with chgrp-like group logic)."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"28576ec6-2aa4-4dfd-9a4a-73f493f2dc46","uuid":"aed5d084-4292-481d-86ba-d50b805b3206","timestamp":"2026-05-24T01:28:42.820Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need to read several files for implementing cmd/chown. Please read and return the full contents of:\n\n1. docs/specs/software-requirements/srd091-chown.yaml\n2. cmd/chmod/main.go\n3. cmd/chgrp/main.go\n4. cmd/chgrp/chgrp_test.go\n\nThese are in the repo at /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5555/\n\nI need the full file contents of each.","agentId":"abeeac2e8acdb7356","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I've successfully read all four files. Here's a summary of what you have:\n\n## File Contents Summary\n\n**1. docs/specs/software-requirements/srd091-chown.yaml**\nThis is the Software Requirements Document for implementing `cmd/chown`. It specifies:\n- Must support ownership specification with OWNER[:GROUP] syntax, including numeric IDs\n- Must support --reference=RFILE to match another file's ownership\n- Must implement recursive (-R) and symlink handling flags (-h, -H, -L, -P)\n- Must support verbose (-v), changes (-c), and silent (-f) output modes\n- Exit code 0 on success, 1 on any error\n- Must handle SIGPIPE gracefull