{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via the cobbler orchestrator) has assigned Task #5555: implement `cmd/chown` for the go-unix-utils project. Specifically, this task covers only srd091 requirements R1.1 through R1.4 — the core ownership-change functionality and argument parsing. The scope is:\n   - R1.1: Parse command-line flags and OWNER[:GROUP] FILE... argument structure\n   - R1.2: Resolve OWNER to numeric UID and optional GROUP to numeric GID (supporting both names and numeric IDs)\n   - R1.3: Apply ownership change to each specified file using os.Chown\n   - R1.4: Install SIGPIPE handler via sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() and support --help and --version flags\n   \n   NOT in scope: recursive (-R), --reference, symlink handling (-h/-H/-L/-P), verbose (-v), changes (-c), silent (-f) — these are R2.x and R3.x requirements for a separate task.\n\n   Files to create: `cmd/chown/main.go` and `cmd/chown/chown_test.go`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - GNU chown OWNER[:GROUP] parsing: supports OWNER, OWNER:GROUP, OWNER:, :GROUP forms\n   - os/user.Lookup for name-to-UID resolution, os/user.LookupGroup for name-to-GID resolution\n   - os.Chown for applying ownership changes\n   - Differential testing pattern using pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests against Homebrew's `gchown` reference binary\n   - SIGPIPE handling via pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n   - Copyright header required on all Go files\n   - 40-line function limit, 500-line file limit (execution constitution rules E8, E9)\n   - No git commands — orchestrator manages git externally\n   - Write all files before building/testing (no incremental compile-fix loops)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd091-chown.yaml** (READ via agent — summary only)\n     - Defines all chown requirements: R1.1-R1.4 (core, in scope), R2.1-R2.3 (recursive/reference/symlink, out of scope), R3.1-R3.3 (verbose/changes/silent, out of scope)\n     - Non-goals: --preserve-root, --from conditional changes\n     - Exit code 0 on success, 1 on any error\n   \n   - **cmd/chgrp/main.go** (READ via agent — summary only, key reference implementation)\n     - Closely related to chown (chgrp changes group only, chown changes owner+group)\n     - Pattern: resolveGID, lookupGroup, gidToName helpers\n     - Uses os.Lchown/os.Chown with symlink mode logic\n     - chownSingle for non-recursive, chownRecursive for -R\n     - shouldFollowLink for -H/-L/-P flags\n     - printDiagnostic and reportError functions\n     - Uses sys.Stat and sys.Lstat for cross-platform file info\n\n   - **cmd/chgrp/chgrp_test.go** (READ via agent — summary only)\n     - Differential testing against gchgrp reference binary\n     - Tests: basic changes, numeric GIDs, multiple files, references, recursion, symlinks, output modes, error cases\n     - Helper functions: testGroups, setGroup, verifyGroup, normalizeBinaryName, sortLines\n     - Reset functions to return files to original state between runs\n\n   - **cmd/chmod/main.go** (READ via agent — summary only)\n     - Another reference implementation for permission/ownership utilities\n     - Parses arguments into options, mode, files\n     - Supports -v, -c, -f, -R, --reference flags\n     - applyAndReport function, formatErr for error formatting\n\n   - **cmd/chown/main.go** — TO BE CREATED\n   - **cmd/chown/chown_test.go** — TO BE CREATED\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. No code has been written. Only research was performed via an Explore agent.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - The Explore agent was launched to gather reference implementations and the SRD. It returned summaries of 4 files (srd091-chown.yaml, cmd/chmod/main.go, cmd/chgrp/main.go, cmd/chgrp/chgrp_test.go).\n   - Key insight