ils.BuildBinary + exec.LookPath(\"gchown\") + testutils.RunDiffTests\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Read the full file contents of cmd/chgrp/main.go and cmd/chgrp/chgrp_test.go (the closest reference implementations), then read the full SRD at docs/specs/software-requirements/srd091-chown.yaml to get the exact requirement text and acceptance criteria for R1.1-R1.4. Then write both cmd/chown/main.go and cmd/chown/chown_test.go in one pass before building and testing.\n\n   The task description says: \"Implement srd091 R1.1: parse command-line flags and the OWNER[:GROUP] FILE... argument structure per the SRD\", \"Implement srd091 R1.2: resolve OWNER to numeric UID and optional GROUP to numeric GID\", \"Implement srd091 R1.3: apply ownership change to each specified file using the resolved UID and GID via os.Chown\", \"Implement srd091 R1.4: install SIGPIPE handler via sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() and support --help and --version flags\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5555/28576ec6-2aa4-4dfd-9a4a-73f493f2dc46.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"28576ec6-2aa4-4dfd-9a4a-73f493f2dc46","uuid":"161c5bbd-5ff2-4f8f-bc9a-269db519b959","timestamp":"2026-05-24T01:29:49.179Z","isSynthetic":true}
